tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-405-a-nested-fixed-array-outside-a-group-is-told-once.hero:22:12: error[ffi_field_type]: `i32[2][3]` cannot be a field of a `record` in an `extern` group — the header owns the layout, and it can hold a number, `bool`, `ptr`, `cstr`, or another record of the group (§4.19)
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-405-a-nested-fixed-array-outside-a-group-is-told-once.hero:23:25: error[ffi_type]: `i64[2][3]` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (§4.19)
